  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 24,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.67,
            0.048,
            0.861,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Tales by Dots and Lines"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.087,
            0.825,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Share your observations on this graph. What do you find interesting?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.113,
            0.847,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Unlike the earlier graphs that were made up of a few connected line segments, this line graph looks like a smooth curve because it contains 80 data points that are placed very close to each other. Representing the same data using a column graph would require 70 columns, making the graph look cluttered and heavy. A line graph is a better choice here. It is light and captures the pattern well."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.223,
            0.847,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From the graph we can see that the average sleep time for 6-year olds is about 9.5 hours per day. The daily sleep time decreases as we grow through teenage years and step into adulthood, touching about 8 hours a day between ages 30 and 50. After 50, the daily sleep time increases, reaching about 8.5 hours."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.314,
            0.847,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You might wonder — why do newborns and infants sleep for so long? Do people in different countries sleep differently? Do animals also exhibit such patterns in sleep durations across age?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.379,
            0.295,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.404,
            0.314,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Mean Grids:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.427,
            0.741,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Fill the grid with 9 distinct numbers such that the average along each row, column, and diagonal is 10."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.47,
            0.741,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Can we fill the grid by changing a few numbers and still get 10 as the average in all directions?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.759,
            0.407,
            0.893,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.759,
                0.407,
                0.893,
                0.511
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_24_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.519,
            0.847,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Give two examples of data that satisfy each of the following conditions:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.561,
            0.517,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) 3 numbers whose mean is 8."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.585,
            0.561,
            0.605
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) 4 numbers whose median is 15.5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.609,
            0.543,
            0.628
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) 5 numbers whose mean is 13.6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.633,
            0.572,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) 6 numbers whose mean = median."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.657,
            0.572,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) 6 numbers whose mean > median."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.686,
            0.847,
            0.744
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Fill in the blanks such that the median of the collection is 13: 5, 21, 14, . How many possibilities exist if only counting numbers are allowed?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.753,
            0.847,
            0.81
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Fill in the blanks such that the mean of the collection is 6.5: 3, 11, _, 15, 6. How many possibilities exist if only counting numbers are allowed?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.819,
            0.846,
            0.858
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Check whether each of the statements below is true. Justify your reasoning. Use algebra, if necessary, to justify."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.862,
            0.647,
            0.882
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) The average of two even numbers is even."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.885,
            0.822,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) The average of any two multiples of 5 will be a multiple of 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.909,
            0.84,
            0.931
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) The average of any 5 multiples of 5 will also be a multiple of 5."
            }
          ]
        },
